## Vite admin SPA build output — derived from DorkNet.Server/admin-ui/
## via `npm run build` (local) or the admin-ui Dockerfile stage (deploy).
## Each build emits a new hash (assets/index-<hash>.js) so committing
## these files leaves a stale index.html → JS hash mismatch the next
## time someone rebuilds. Keep the source committed, regenerate output.
DorkNet.Server/wwwroot/admin/index.html
DorkNet.Server/wwwroot/admin/assets/
DorkNet.Server/wwwroot/admin/*.map
DorkNet.Server/admin-ui/node_modules/
DorkNet.Server/admin-ui/dist/
DorkNet.Server/admin-ui/.vite/
DorkNet.Server/admin-ui/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

## Public-facing site (Vite + React, DorkNet.Server/site/)
## Same reasoning as admin-ui above: hashed output, regenerate per build.
DorkNet.Server/wwwroot/site/index.html
DorkNet.Server/wwwroot/site/assets/
DorkNet.Server/wwwroot/site/*.map
DorkNet.Server/site/node_modules/
DorkNet.Server/site/dist/
DorkNet.Server/site/.vite/
DorkNet.Server/site/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
